# roles.default — which local model does which job (deployed by Linux_Theme). To make it yours, copy it to
# ~/code/custom_models/roles.conf — your private custom_models repo, which a reinstall clones back — or,
# for this machine only, to roles.conf beside this file (wins over both). The installer touches neither.
# After an edit: systemctl --user restart fox-llm-server && fox-llm-update --sync
#
# Columns: role  model (its Ollama name — the file is read from Ollama's store)  server (llama | ollama)
#   agent  pi / opencode / the fox-symdeps explain cards (they follow pi) — long context, tools
#   quick  short chat, inline edits — small enough for a 4 GB GPU
#   fim    Copilot-style ghost text — a BASE coder model: instruct ones run past the cursor
#   title  opencode session titles
#   embed  embeddings (fask, findex) — what libfox-intel embeds with
agent  qwen3-coder:30b           llama
quick  qwen2.5-coder:7b          llama
fim    qwen2.5-coder:1.5b-base   llama
title  qwen2.5:3b                llama
embed  mxbai-embed-large         llama
